// Practice quiz: The box model
// Formative, low-stakes retention practice. Titles name the objective id each item practises.

$CATEGORY: html-css-js/html-and-css/the-box-model

::o1 where the background shows::A box has a blue background, padding 10px and margin 30px. Where does the blue appear? {
=In the content and padding areas, up to the border #Correct. The background fills the content and padding; margin is transparent space outside the border.
~In the margin as well #Not quite. Margin is always transparent and shows the parent's background.
~Only behind the text #Not quite. The background also shows through the padding.
~Only in the border #Not quite. The border has its own color; the background sits inside it.
}

::o2 content-box width::With the default box-sizing, an element has width 300px, padding 15px and border 1px on every side. How wide is it on screen? {
=332px #Correct. Under content-box, 300 + 15 + 15 + 1 + 1 \= 332.
~300px #Not quite. That would be the result under border-box.
~316px #Not quite. Padding and border apply on both sides, so each is counted twice.
~362px #Not quite. Margin is not part of the rendered width, and nothing here adds 30 more.
}

::o2 border-box width::An element has box-sizing border-box, width 300px, padding 15px and border 1px. How wide is its content area? {
=268px #Correct. Under border-box the 300px includes padding and border, so the content gets 300 - 30 - 2 \= 268px.
~300px #Not quite. That is the whole box; padding and border take space inside it.
~332px #Not quite. That is the content-box total.
~285px #Not quite. Padding and border are on both sides.
}

::o3 sibling margins::A heading has margin-bottom 24px and the paragraph after it has margin-top 16px, in normal block layout. How big is the gap? {
=24px #Correct. Adjacent vertical margins of blocks collapse into the larger one.
~40px #Not quite. The margins do not add up; they collapse.
~16px #Not quite. The collapsed margin is the larger of the two, not the smaller.
~0px #Not quite. Collapsing keeps one margin; it does not remove both.
}

::o3 flex items::The same heading and paragraph sit inside a container with display flex and flex-direction column. How big is the gap now? {
=40px #Correct. Margins of flex items do not collapse, so 24 + 16 \= 40px.
~24px #Not quite. Collapse happens in block layout; flex items keep both margins.
~16px #Not quite. No margin is dropped in a flex container.
~0px #Not quite. Flex layout keeps the margins.
}
